# Play a full Sverdle guess: click letters, then submit via a SvelteKit form
# action (use:enhance -> fetch POST). Game state lives in a cookie.
#
# App observation: the board tiles are anonymous divs — the only semantic
# observable while typing is the enter button's enablement (it arms after the
# 5th letter). Per-letter tile assertions are not expressible; a screen-reader
# user gets equally little per-keystroke feedback.
flow "sverdle first guess"

go /sverdle
  expect heading "Sverdle"
  expect count text "empty" 30
  expect disabled button "enter"

click button "a"
  expect disabled button "enter"

click button "b"
  expect disabled button "enter"

click button "o"
  expect disabled button "enter"

click button "u"
  expect disabled button "enter"

click button "t"
  expect enabled button "enter"

click button "enter"
  expect request POST /sverdle ok
  expect count text "empty" 25
  expect disabled button "enter"
